On May 17, 1:48 pm, Haakon Studebaker <hepta...@gmail.com> wrote:
> Is it possible to have too many patches in NetHack? I just tried to apply a
> 26th patch and the game panics. Boy am I glad that I backed up.

no, it is not possible to have "too manypatches" in Nethack.

I was going to type a long dissertation on what a patch actually does,
and why it is difficult to apply multiple patches, but i'm lazy. The
long and short of it is: it's difficult to apply multiple patches
because they assume they are being applied only to the original/
official nethack source. If you are trying to apply a patch to some
source code that is drastically different than the original/official
nethack source code then things get tricky and the "patch" executable
can get confused. It will take a lot of manual hand-tuning to make
things work right.

it's a good idea to make backups before applying any patch, on your
1st or on your 25th. It seems like you did this - good job. To apply
the 25th patch just be careful to make sure all #ifdef's line up, all
the brackets { } () line up, and any return statements are kosher. You
can check this manually when you apply the patch - it might be tedius
depending on the size of the patch.

I'm suspect that it wasn't just the 26th one that screwed things up -
when applying multiple patches i could see little errors creeping up
in each successive patch, not necessarily all of them working fine
until one big failure. But hopefully i'm wrong =)

